    "title": "AAA expects record breaking 5.7 million Texas travelers during Fourth of July weekend - NewsBreak",
    "text": "TYLER, Texas ( KETK ) — AAA is expecting to see a new record of around 5.7 million Texans travel during Fourth of July weekend this year. AAA projects that around 5.7 million Texans will travel at least 50 miles over the holiday weekend period which lasts from June 28 to July 6. According to AAA, the domestic travel forecast shows an increase of 360,000 Texans travelers from last year. If these projections are correct, the increase would amount to 521,000 more Texans than seen in 2019. The domestic travel forecast is based off a two weekend period to achieve a more accurate statistics on the flow of holiday travelers. You can now stream KETK and FOX51 News live 24/7 on your smart TV with KETK+ , our brand-new app! No antenna, cable, or satellite needed— watch for free, anytime. Just download it on your Roku, Apple TV, or Fire TV and start streaming. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KETK.com | FOX51.com.",
